## Reviewer disagreements (not applied as suggested)
- fi-a 20 and fi-b 24. Space thousands are what Finnish typography wants. The checker and ACCEPTED-ROUND do not accept them. Period grouping kept.
- fi-a 22 and fi-b 26. The fragments are in the Korean source (same ZWSP counts). Removing them or making new headings fails the checker. Layout left.
- fi-a 21, except "1 päivää kohden". The other "1"s are statutory counts. "yksi" alone is not in the Finnish number lexicon, so replacing the digit with a word would fail the number check.
- fi-a 1, the aside about 004 "(10 artikla)" and URL flno=3. English and Korean 004 name article 10 of the business-tax act. flno=3 is the database fragment, not the article number. Dropping 10 would fail the checker. 001's label for the same URL is now "Säännös liikevaihtoveron yleisestä verokannasta". 004 still says "10 artikla". URL unchanged.
